{
  "summary": "This study investigates closed nanopores in silicon-carbon anodes as stress-regulation units to mitigate lithiation-induced deformation and interphase degradation. By engineering heteroatom-doped carbon hosts with abundant closed pores, the research redirects expansion stress inward, suppresses electrode swelling, and enhances Li+ kinetics. The nitrogen-doped composite achieves 1756.5 mAh g-1 capacity, 90.2% initial Coulombic efficiency, and 868.4 mAh g-1 at 3 C, reducing thickness expansion from 38.4% to 13.1% after 50 cycles. The approach demonstrates scalability for practical battery anodes.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Closed nanopores in heteroatom-doped carbon hosts redirect lithiation-induced stress inward, suppressing electrode swelling",
    "Nitrogen-doped silicon-carbon composites achieve 1756.5 mAh g-1 reversible capacity and 90.2% initial Coulombic efficiency",
    "The design reduces thickness expansion from 38.4% to 13.1% after 50 cycles and enables scalable production for 2 Ah NCM811 pouch cells"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes closed-pore stress regulation as a scalable structural strategy for practical low-expansion silicon-carbon anodes, addressing mechanical instability in high-energy lithium-ion batteries."
}

{
  "summary": "This study integrated single-cell epigenomic data from 2.5 million adult mouse brain nuclei, profiling four histone modifications, transcriptomes, chromatin accessibility, DNA methylation, and 3D genome organization. The resulting atlas identified 100+ cell subclasses and defined active, primed, and repressive chromatin states across 81% of the genome. Active states with combinatorial histone marks better predict functional enhancers than accessibility alone, while H3K27me3 and H3K9me3 define repressive mechanisms. The resource enables deep learning models for predicting epigenomic features and gene expression from DNA sequence.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The atlas spans over 100 brain cell subclasses using integrated epigenomic profiling",
    "Active chromatin states marked by combinatorial histone modifications better predict functional enhancers than chromatin accessibility alone",
    "H3K27me3- and H3K9me3-marked chromatin states delineate distinct modes of cell-type-specific gene repression"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This multimodal resource provides a comprehensive framework for annotating the brain regulatory genome and interpreting non-coding disease risk variants through integrated epigenomic mapping."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates a dual-copper catalytic system enabling switchable chlorine atom transfer radical reactions. It uses unactivated alk. chlorides to perform atom transfer radical addition (ATRA) and atom transfer radical polymerization (ATRP) by selectively activating C-Cl bonds and switching reaction pathways based on catalyst presence. The approach allows synthesis of diverse small molecules and α-end-functionalized polyacrylates while modifying PVC under mild conditions.",
  "key_findings": [
    "A dinuclear copper complex activates unactivated alkyl chlorides for C-Cl bond cleavage",
    "Mononuclear copper catalyst enables controllable C-Cl bond reconstruction",
    "Switchable pathway between ATRA and ATRP reactions via catalyst presence"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a versatile platform for chlorine atom transfer radical reactions using unactivated organochlorides, advancing synthetic and polymer chemistry by enabling mild modification of PVC and diverse functionalized products."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated how protein kinase A (PKA) signaling regulates group 3 innate lymphoid cell (ILC3) homeostasis and inflammation in the gut. Using a single-cell atlas, researchers found that prostaglandin activates PKA to promote tissue-protective functions, while interleukin-23 (IL-23) suppresses PKA inhibitors. Deletion of PRKAR1A reduced ILC3s and increased infection susceptibility in mice. IL-23 overproduction decreased PRKAR1A, increasing PKA signaling and gut inflammation. Human ILC3s express PRKAR1A, which is downregulated by IL-23 or in inflammatory bowel disease.",
  "key_findings": [
    "ILC3s maintain gut homeostasis via PKA signaling regulated by PRKAR1A",
    "IL-23 suppresses PKA inhibitors to reduce ILC3s and increase infection susceptibility",
    "IL-23 overproduction decreases PRKAR1A, driving PKA-mediated gut inflammation"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes PKA signaling as a critical regulator of ILC3-mediated gut homeostasis, with IL-23 acting as a key driver of pathological PKA activation in inflammation."
}

{
  "summary": "This study examines recent high-impact publications across Science journals to identify patterns in research output and thematic trends. The analysis approached the problem by categorizing articles by field and publication year, revealing shifts in interdisciplinary collaboration and emerging research areas. Key findings indicate increased cross-disciplinary work and notable growth in specific scientific domains.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Increased cross-disciplinary collaboration in recent years",
    "Emergence of new research domains within Science journals",
    "Shifts in thematic focus across publication years"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The analysis provides a snapshot of evolving research landscapes in high-impact science, highlighting how interdisciplinary trends and domain-specific growth inform the trajectory of scientific discovery."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates kinetic-environmental coupling at buried interfaces in ambient flexible perovskite solar cells. Using dual-side in situ photoluminescence, researchers discovered simultaneous nucleation at gas-liquid and liquid-solid interfaces during antisolvent processing. Outward solvent evaporation delays α-phase conversion at the buried interface, causing kinetic mismatch that worsens moisture damage. The authors designed a self-segregating molecule (NFA) that enriches at the buried interface to synchronize crystallization, passivate defects, optimize energy alignment, and form a hydrophobic barrier. This approach achieved record ambient flexible efficiencies (24.84% for small cells, 21.46% for mini-modules) with stable performance after 1000h damp aging at 85±5% RH.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Simultaneous nucleation occurs at both gas-liquid and liquid-solid interfaces during antisolvent processing",
    "Outward solvent evaporation delays α-phase conversion at the buried interface, exacerbating moisture damage",
    "Self-segregating molecule NFA synchronizes crystallization, passivates defects, optimizes energy alignment, and forms a hydrophobic barrier"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes self-segregated interfacial regulation as a rational strategy to overcome kinetic-environmental constraints in scalable flexible photovoltaics."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates whether freshwater availability alone explains early human settlement patterns in desert regions. Using a 1,500-km geoarchaeological survey across the Rub' al Khali desert, researchers found that the presence of knappable stone for tool production was a critical factor alongside water. Palaeolake deposits indicated water access at 55 of 125 sites, but no lithic artefacts or raw materials were present where stone was absent. The analysis shows settlement required co-occurrence of water and lithic resources, with 57% of water-accessible terrain lacking suitable stone. This suggests that raw-material geology significantly constrains human dispersal, challenging models that prioritize water availability.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Palaeolake deposits were present at 55 of 125 surveyed sites, indicating water access but no lithic raw materials in the absence of stone",
    "Settlement patterns required co-occurrence of water and knappable stone, with 57% of water-accessible terrain lacking suitable stone",
    "Spatial modeling shows raw-material availability improves discrimination of site locations by 0.695 to 0.768, indicating significant constraint on dispersal"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The findings demonstrate that lithic raw material availability, not water alone, critically constrained early human dispersal across arid regions, challenging prevailing models of human settlement in deserts."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates Papaver self-incompatibility (SI) by identifying two alternative polymorphic S genes, SOPT and SGRP, which function as idiomorphs when the previously known PrpS-PrsS pair is absent. The researchers confirmed these genes confer SI in Arabidopsis thaliana, revealing a dual-idiomorph system with no shared ancestry. This finding demonstrates a distinct genetic basis for SI polymorphism in Papaver.",
  "key_findings": [
    "SOPT and S.GRP genes function as alternative S determinants in Papaver rhoeas when PrpS-PrsS is absent",
    "Both genes confer self-incompatibility when heterologously expressed in Arabidopsis thaliana",
    "The Papaver SI system operates via two multiallelic idiomorphs with no obvious common ancestry"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This discovery reveals a dual-idiomorph system for self-incompatibility in Papaver, providing a distinct genetic basis for polymorphism in allorecognition mechanisms."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates shear alignment polymer extrusion (SHAPE) 3D printing for fabricating high-loading nanocomposites with long-range ordered nanostructures. The approach uses high shear forces to align nanofillers like boron nitride nanosheets and carbon nanotubes in polymer matrices, enabling scalable production of complex 3D architectures. Results show 55 wt% boron nitride in polylactic acid filaments achieve zero volume shrinkage post-sintering, with tailored thermal conductivity (1.07 W/m/K) and mechanical properties for thermal management and structural applications.",
  "key_findings": [
    "SHAPE 3D printing enables high-loading nanocomposites (up to 55 wt% boron nitride) with long-range ordered nanostructures",
    "Post-sintering yields zero volume shrinkage and exceptional thermomechanical stability for temperatures above polymer melting",
    "Vertically aligned composites exhibit enhanced thermal conductivity (1.07 W/m/K), while horizontally aligned structures provide thermal insulation (0.071 W/m/K)"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This method bridges nanoscale nanofiller ordering and macroscale functionality in high-loading composites, advancing cross-scale design for thermal management and structural materials."
}

{
  "summary": "This study developed human renal cell carcinoma assembloids to model tumour-CAF-T cell interactions. By reconstituting cancer cells, CAFs, and immune cells, it revealed CAFs coordinate CD8+ T cell stemness via WNT-induced activin A, enhancing anti-PD-1 therapy response. The findings identify a tumour-CAF-T cell axis governing heterogeneous immune checkpoint inhibitor responses and provide a platform for personalized immunotherapy evaluation.",
  "key_findings": [
    "CAF-mediated CD8+ T cell stemness maintained through WNT-driven activin A expression",
    "Tumour-CAF-T cell axis determines heterogeneous responses to anti-PD-1 therapy",
    "WNT-unresponsive CAFs cause activin A deficiency and therapy resistance"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a mechanistic tumour-CAF-T cell axis that explains heterogeneous immune checkpoint inhibitor responses, advancing understanding of renal cancer microenvironment dynamics and immunotherapy resistance mechanisms."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated whether a messenger RNA vaccine developed by Merck and Moderna reduces melanoma recurrence risk. The research analyzed clinical trial data showing the vaccine significantly lowers the risk of melanoma recurrence compared to placebo. However, the underlying mechanisms and long-term efficacy remain unclear, leaving critical questions unresolved.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The mRNA vaccine reduced melanoma recurrence risk in clinical trials",
    "The vaccine demonstrated efficacy against melanoma recurrence",
    "The study identified unresolved questions about mechanisms and long-term effects"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The findings provide evidence for an mRNA vaccine's potential in melanoma prevention, highlighting the need for further research into its mechanisms and durability."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the long-standing challenge of achieving stable photocatalytic pure water splitting over Ta3N5 by identifying incompatibility in cocatalysts between alkaline water oxidation systems and pure water splitting as a critical bottleneck. A highly dispersed RuCoOx cocatalyst was developed using multi-step incipient wetness impregnation. The optimized Pt@Cr2O3/Ta3N5/RuCoOx photocatalyst achieves stoichiometric water splitting with an apparent quantum yield of 0.72% at 420 nm, the highest reported for Ta-based nitrides. Mechanistic insights indicate enhanced interfacial electric fields and reduced reaction barriers improve hole extraction and intermediate kinetics.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Identification of cocatalyst incompatibility between alkaline water oxidation and pure water splitting as a bottleneck for Ta3N5 photocatalysis",
    "Development of a highly dispersed RuCoOx cocatalyst via multi-step incipient wetness impregnation",
    "Optimized Pt@Cr2O3/Ta3N5/RuCoOx achieves 0.72% apparent quantum yield for stoichiometric water splitting at 420 nm"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes cocatalyst compatibility as a fundamental design principle for stable photocatalytic water splitting in nitride-based materials, providing mechanistic insights for advancing solar-driven water splitting technologies."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated somatic copy number variants (CNVs) in human cortical neurons across development. Using single-cell whole-genome sequencing from fetal to postnatal brain tissue, researchers found that 25.9% of prenatal cortical neurons had widespread CNVs. Postnatal elimination reduced this proportion by ~4.5-fold, with defective neurons selectively eliminated perinatally. Surviving neurons showed depletion of dosage-sensitive genes and neurodevelopmental disorder genes, indicating a quality-control mechanism that may impact neurodevelopmental disease susceptibility.",
  "key_findings": [
    "25.9% of prenatal cortical neurons exhibited widespread copy number variants",
    "Perinatal elimination reduced CNV-positive neurons by ~4.5-fold compared to prenatal levels",
    "Surviving neurons showed depletion of dosage-sensitive genes and neurodevelopmental disorder genes"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study reveals a perinatal genome quality-control mechanism that eliminates neurons with aberrant genomes, potentially explaining the genetic basis of neurodevelopmental disorders through selective elimination of neurons with dosage-sensitive genomic anomalies."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated whether emerging technologies could permanently eliminate PFAS chemicals from the environment. The research assessed potential remediation methods to address PFAS contamination, which are pervasive and persistent in ecosystems. The findings indicate that current technological approaches lack the capacity to achieve complete PFAS removal, highlighting the urgent need for innovative solutions to mitigate their environmental persistence.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Current remediation technologies cannot achieve complete PFAS removal",
    "PFAS chemicals are highly persistent in ecosystems",
    "Existing methods fail to address PFAS contamination effectively"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study underscores the critical challenge of PFAS environmental persistence and the necessity for novel technological advancements to achieve permanent remediation."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates phase crystallization control in cesium lead bromide perovskites for efficient light-emitting diodes. Using additive-mediated sequential crystallization with 3-carboxyphenylphosphonic acid, researchers decoupled 0D Cs4PbBr6 and 3D CsPbBr3 phases. The approach enhanced CsPbBr3 film quality and surface morphology, achieving nearly 100% photoluminescence quantum yield and 35.3% external quantum efficiency in green PeLEDs.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Sequential crystallization of Cs4PbBr6 and CsPbBr3 phases via additive-mediated strategy",
    "Improved CsPbBr3 film quality and surface morphology enabling high light outcoupling",
    "Ultrahigh photoluminescence quantum yield (nearly 100%) and 35.3% external quantum efficiency in green PeLEDs"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates that precise phase crystallization engineering can overcome phase mixing challenges in perovskite light-emitters, enabling near-unity photoluminescence efficiency and high external quantum efficiency for practical optoelectronic applications."
}

{
  "summary": "This study isolates two archaeal strains (HC1 and SC1) from Heimdallarchaeia, the lineage closest to eukaryotes. These obligately anaerobic, syntrophic archaea lack persistent internal membranes but produce protrusions and vesicles. Comparative genomics indicates Cox genes support oxygen detoxification rather than respiration, suggesting the archaeal ancestor of eukaryotes may have possessed anaerobic features with early oxygen adaptation mechanisms.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Isolation of Heimdallarchaeia strains HC1 and SC1 as the closest archaeal relatives to eukaryotes",
    "These archaea lack persistent internal membranes but exhibit membrane protrusions and vesicles",
    "Cox genes in these strains support oxygen detoxification, not respiration, indicating early oxygen adaptation mechanisms"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The findings provide direct evidence that the archaeal ancestor of eukaryotes likely possessed anaerobic physiological features with early oxygen detoxification mechanisms, advancing understanding of eukaryogenesis through cultivation-informed archaeal models."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates whether AI chatbots could inadvertently disclose sensitive scientific research to competitors. Researchers analyzed potential vulnerabilities in AI systems that might leak confidential information. The findings suggest that without specific safeguards, AI interactions may unintentionally expose research details, highlighting risks in using such tools for sensitive scientific communication.",
  "key_findings": [
    "AI chatbots may unintentionally leak confidential research information during interactions",
    "Current AI systems lack sufficient safeguards to prevent accidental disclosure of sensitive data",
    "This poses risks for researchers sharing confidential scientific information via AI platforms"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study identifies critical vulnerabilities in AI communication systems that could compromise research confidentiality, advancing understanding of information security risks in emerging AI technologies."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how engineered excited-state coupling in binuclear copper iodide clusters enhances exciton harvesting for scintillation. Using isomeric Cu-I clusters with similar x-ray attenuation, the researchers identified that intermolecular coupling accelerates carrier relaxation and improves radiative recombination. The findings enabled water-resistant scintillator glasses achieving 32,456 photons MeV-. The work offers mechanistic insights for designing efficient cluster-based scintillators.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Engineered excited-state coupling accelerates carrier relaxation in binuclear copper iodide clusters",
    "Isomeric clusters with identical x-ray attenuation coefficients revealed intermolecular coupling's role in exciton harvesting",
    "Water-resistant scintillator glasses achieved 32,456 photons MeV-1 light yield and 33.6 lp mm-1 spatial resolution"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a mechanistic framework for optimizing exciton harvesting in metal-cluster scintillators through engineered excited-state coupling, advancing the design of high-performance, environmentally benign x-ray imaging materials."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated whether emotion regulation capacity shares a common neural signature using cognitive reappraisal as a measure. Analyzing 40 fMRI datasets from 2,175 participants, it found that three indicators of reappraisal capacity—trait questionnaires, task-based affective ratings, and amygdala down-regulation—lack convergence on a single neural core. None showed expected links with prefrontal regulatory circuits, challenging the assumption that such brain activity reflects emotion regulation ability.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Three indicators of reappraisal capacity do not converge on a shared neural signature",
    "None of the indicators showed associations with canonical prefrontal regulatory circuits",
    "Task-based affective ratings were linked to amygdala and sensorimotor cortices rather than regulatory regions"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The findings challenge the assumption that prefrontal regulatory circuit activation reliably indicates emotion regulation capacity, suggesting neural biomarkers for this trait must account for non-specific neural engagement during emotional processing."
}

{
  "summary": "This study maps global threats to freshwater biodiversity by assessing 45 threats across 21,490 species. It reveals that highly developed and water-managed regions experience multiple overlapping threats, increasing extinction risk and population declines. Freshwater species face higher threat intensity and distinct spatial patterns compared to terrestrial species, providing a baseline for targeted conservation interventions.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Highly developed and water-managed regions experience multiple overlapping threats",
    "Increasing threat probabilities elevate extinction risk and population declines in freshwater species",
    "Freshwater species exhibit greater threat intensity and distinct spatial patterns than terrestrial species"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study establishes a spatially explicit baseline for prioritizing freshwater conservation interventions by quantifying threat impacts across global freshwater biodiversity."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates polyzwitterion-based organic photoelectric synaptic transistors for neuromorphic vision applications. By using poly(3-(1-vinyl-3-imidazolyl)-proaphenylsulfonate) as a single dielectric layer, the researchers stabilized ionic charges and suppressed ion-migration. The devices achieved ultralow power consumption (10.95 aJ) and demonstrated multicolor robot vision, pedestrian recognition, and motion prediction capabilities.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Polyzwitterion dielectric layer stabilizes ionic charges and prevents ion-migration",
    "Devices achieved ultralow event energy consumption (10.95 aJ)",
    "Supported multicolor robot vision, pedestrian recognition, and motion prediction"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work advances neuromorphic vision hardware by integrating photoelectric sensing and synaptic plasticity in a single ultralow-power device architecture."
}

{
  "summary": "This study visualizes subcycle electron dynamics in graphene using attosecond-precision techniques, capturing coherent Landau-Zener-Majorana transitions across the entire first Brillouin zone. It demonstrates non-thermal electron distributions and reveals how strong-field acceleration interacts with interband tunnusing periodic Landau-Zener-Majorana processes. The method enables unprecedented microscopic insights into strong-field quantum control mechanisms.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Attosecond-precision subcycle band-structure videography visualizes Landau-Zener-Majorana transitions in graphene across the full first Brillouin zone",
    "Strong-field-driven electron acceleration in graphene exhibits non-thermal distributions due to periodic Landau-Zener-Majorana interband tunnelling",
    "The technique disentangles competing scattering processes to assess coherent electronic control mechanisms"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a direct visualization method for lightwave-driven electron motion in quantum materials, advancing understanding of strong-field quantum processes through subcycle resolution."
}

{
  "summary": "This study examines the NIH's selection process for a mental health institute director, focusing on the alignment of candidates with metabolic psychiatry expertise. The research identifies a candidate with strong MAHA-aligned leadership in this specialized field. The findings indicate a shift toward prioritizing metabolic psychiatry in mental health research leadership.",
  "key_findings": [
    "A candidate with MAHA-aligned leadership in metabolic psychiatry was selected for the NIH mental health institute director role",
    "The study highlights the growing emphasis on metabolic psychiatry within mental health research leadership",
    "The selection process prioritizes candidates with expertise in metabolic psychiatry for mental health institute leadership"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study provides insight into evolving leadership priorities in mental health research, particularly the increasing focus on metabolic psychiatry as a critical domain."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates targeting the ER stress-ROS-inflammation cycle in periodontitis using a novel heterojunction biomaterial. The approach combines cobalt susing taurine to scavenge ROS, disrupt bacterial metabolism, restore redox balance, and alleviate ER stress. Results show enhanced osteogenic differentiation in human periodontal ligament cells and reduced alveolar bone resorption in models, indicating effective cycle disruption for tissue repair.",
  "key_findings": [
    "ERR-HJ disrupts bacterial respiration via ROS scavenging and electron transfer from H2O2",
    "Taurine-containing heterojunction restores redox balance and alleviates ER stress by dampening PERK-CHOP pathway",
    "ERR-HJ promotes osteogenic differentiation of human periodontal ligament cells and reduces bone resorption in periodontitis models"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study provides a mechanism for simultaneously targeting bacterial infection and the ER stress-ROS-inflammation cycle, offering a template for biomaterials that integrate antimicrobial action with tissue regeneration in periodontitis."
}
